From: Project Calamansi
Subject: [PATCH] oppo6765: add isolated ARM64 XNU compile profile

This enables an OPPO6765 XNU compile target using Cortex-A53 baseline
instructions. It deliberately does not add OPPO memory, VA, framebuffer, GIC,
or timer constants. A successful build is compile evidence only; boot support
requires a separately verified CPH2179 handoff and memory profile.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/proc_reg.h b/osfmk/arm64/proc_reg.h
--- a/osfmk/arm64/proc_reg.h
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/proc_reg.h
@@ -220,2 +220,9 @@
+#elif defined (ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_OPPO6765) /* Cortex-A53 */
+
+/* Cortex-A53 instruction and data cache lines are 64 bytes. */
+#define MMU_I_CLINE 6
+
+#define MMU_CLINE   6
+
 #elif defined (VMAPPLE)
 
